          "text": "Exstrophy covering\nATI PED164 specifies sterile nonadherent protection and preparation for immediate surgery; Meyers specifically\nteaches a saline-moistened nonadherent cover. Moisture and materials follow the repair team’s order; do not\nconvert protective covering into dry adherent gauze, pressure, or independent device manipulation.\nProcedure timing\nThe supplied ATI structural chapter includes a 6-24-month orchiopexy context and broader early-repair guidance.\nOther class wording can emphasize earlier correction. These are source/condition contexts, not permission to\ndelay a scheduled referral or a universal age for all GU surgery.\nNephrotic mechanism\nNot every nephrotic case has the same cause or BP pattern. The normal/slightly low BP emphasis applies to\nminimal-change disease; severe edema does not prove adequate circulating volume. Biopsy and albumin/diuretic\nuse depend on the individual course.\nDiet and antibiotics\nAGN fluid, sodium, potassium, and protein restrictions depend on output, overload, and azotemia. UTI drugs\ndepend on age, site, culture, and orders; a lower-tract antibiotic is not automatically appropriate for an ill child with\nupper/systemic infection.\nUnsupported or unresolved claims\nAn unresolved numerical difference is not used as the deciding boundary of a check. A source-limited topic is\nlabeled below rather than claimed as ATI-supported. Age, formulation, route, dose unit, treatment phase,\nprocedure, and prescribed plan remain attached to their context. No unrelated disorders were added as standalone\nlessons."
