          "id": "N-L06-s1",
          "title": "Understand the pattern",
          "body": "Methylphenidate is a central nervous system (CNS) stimulant; Ritalin is a brand name. It increases norepinephrine and dopamine activity in the CNS, helping attention and impulse control. Stimulant does not mean that a child must become more physically active: improving these signaling pathways can improve regulation. The medicine can also suppress appetite, interfere with sleep, and affect pulse or blood pressure. Compare objective measures and behavior with baseline rather than using one observation.",
