          "title": "Understand the pattern",
          "body": "A medicine can help ADHD and still cause a problem that needs attention. Mild appetite reduction or sleep difficulty warrants assessment of trends, nutrition, formulation, timing, and the prescribed plan. Chest pain, concerning palpitations or dysrhythmias, and marked blood-pressure changes require prompt clinical assessment. New hallucinations or paranoia are serious adverse manifestations in the supplied ATI text: discontinue the medication and report immediately. This urgent instruction is different from deciding independently to stop ordinary treatment because school is out.",
