          "id": "N-L11-s1",
          "title": "Understand the pattern",
          "body": "An individualized education program (IEP) organizes eligible school services around assessed needs and goals. The important clinical connection is specific difficulty to targeted support. A child with a reading difficulty may need specialized reading instruction and access supports, while a communication difficulty may warrant speech-language evaluation. OT or other referrals depend on actual functional needs. School services, caregiver activities, and treatment for coexisting conditions can work together; one does not erase the need for another.",
